      "reason": "Configured 27-account monitoring through the Horizon weekly research and AI-engineering digest task: 10 additive-manufacturing/manufacturing-engineering accounts, 5 materials/metallurgy accounts, 6 scientific-AI accounts, and 6 AI-engineering/practical-workflow accounts. All 27 active handles are fetched together on Sunday at 12:00; rotation is disabled. TWIglobal, MFGUSA, ASTMAMCOE, MOOSEFramework, OpenCatalyst, and NatureMaterials remain visibly marked with pending or review evidence; out-of-pool candidates are not silently discarded. Production collection uses only one explicit Scweet search composed of the 27 exact `from:handle` clauses joined by OR: profiles mode is prohibited, there are no topic keywords, no replies, a seven-day UTC window, and no automatic retry or paid upgrade. The earlier structured 27-user search silently returned an empty dataset on 2026-08-16, while the prohibited profile-timeline fallback consumed its global 410-item target on only three accounts' historical timelines. Scweet requires at least 100 dataset items per request and its max_items limit is global per run, not per profile. If a run reaches that global cap without observing all requested account handles, the bridge records an incomplete-coverage error, does not advance the cursor, and excludes the packet from the weekly digest. The local gate dynamically allocates the remaining $4.95 monthly budget across remaining Sunday slots: 328 items for a fresh five-Sunday month, 410 for a fresh four-Sunday month, with a hard monthly limit of 1640 items and a $0.05 reserve. The configured five-run field is only a ceiling for a fresh five-Sunday month; historical test or failed-run reservations do not consume future calendar slots. Scientific-AI content must be related to materials, physical or chemical science, scientific computing, simulation, datasets, or autonomous experiments. AI-engineering content may include technically detailed product and industry updates but excludes advertising, referrals, financing, hiring, cryptocurrency, and unsupported generic opinion. The weekly digest remains review-required and does not promote signals into formal knowledge."
